# GH-X Mockup Framing Gold Standard

The approved Harbor & Home / Gathered Days listing mockup framing is the **default for every future digital product** unless the user explicitly requests a different style.

## Hard rules

- Keep approximately the same camera distance and framing as the approved mockup.
- Show the **entire** planner/binder page with comfortable margins.
- **Never** crop page titles, checklists, tables, forms, or text.
- Buyers must be able to read headings and most page content.
- Close-ups may feel premium but must stay readable — no tighter than gold-standard distance.
- All listing images use this framing/aspect unless a lifestyle scene truly requires otherwise.
- Before `READY_TO_SELL`, verify no text is cut off; regenerate any over-zoomed mockup automatically.

## Implementation (GH-X repo)

- Shared module: `ServiceFlowAI/ghx-smoke-heygen/ghx_image_standard.py`
- Use `fit_page()`, `make_closeup()`, `make_listing_page()`, `assert_ready_to_sell_images()`
- Close-up boxes must keep ≥ **92%** of page width and height visible

```text
❌ BAD: tight crop; titles/footers cut off; extreme zoom
✅ GOOD: full page with margins; headings and body readable
```
